Adobe Core-14 font metrics (APAFML)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vendor/afm/ contains Adobe's 14 PostScript(R) AFM files, unmodified, together
with their licence file MustRead.html. They are vendored by decision #22 of
docs/00-NORTH-STAR.md, whose measurement is docs/20-STANDARD-14-METRICS-SCOPE.md.

  Copyright (c) 1985, 1987, 1989, 1990, 1997 Adobe Systems Incorporated.
  All Rights Reserved.  (Each .afm carries its own copyright line; the years
  differ by file and are retained as Adobe wrote them.)

The licence is APAFML. Its full text is vendor/afm/MustRead.html, which must be
distributed WITH the AFM files and is reproduced there byte-exact, including its
original line endings, because the licence requires that its paragraph not be
modified. In Adobe's words, the files "may be used, copied, and distributed for
any purpose and without charge, with or without modification, provided that all
copyright notices are retained; that the AFM files are not distributed without
this file; that all modifications to this file or any of the AFM files are
prominently noted in the modified file(s); and that this paragraph is not
modified."

Nothing in vendor/afm/ is modified, so no file there carries a modification
note. Anything generated FROM these files would be a modified file and must
carry one. The engine embeds them verbatim with include_str! and parses at
runtime, so no generated table exists today.

APAFML is NOT OSI-approved and is deliberately absent from deny.toml. That
allowlist governs crate licences in the resolved dependency graph; these are
data files and never enter it, the same as the Adobe CMap data described below.
An entry cargo-deny could never match is the "just in case" entry that file's
header forbids. The consequence is stated rather than hidden: a non-OSI-approved
licence is present in this repository and CI is green, because no tool here can
check it. The review is decision #22, this notice, and vendor/afm/README.md.

