--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Adobe CMap resources: NOT PRESENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No Adobe CMap resource files (.bcmap or otherwise) are present in this
repository, so no notice for them is currently required (the Adobe Glyph List
above carries its own).

The M3 plan called for vendoring the ~168 predefined CJK CMaps. They are not
here, and that is a declared decision rather than an oversight: nothing in the
conformance corpus exercises them, and committing binary data that no test
touches means shipping data nobody has verified. A document naming a predefined
CMap is REFUSED with a named error rather than decoded approximately, and the
gap is declared as the limitation code `predefined-cmaps-not-vendored` inside
`assurance.limitations`, on every PDF artifact this engine emits — classify and extract
alike, since both take their list from `backend_limitations()`. This paragraph named an
extract artifact's `not_decoded` list until v2-S13.3; that was M3's spelling, M4 absorbed
the list into the L1 gate, and no artifact has carried the field since. The office readers
do not carry this code at all, and correctly: it names what a PDF backend could not decode.

When those files land — with a fixture that proves they work — they belong under
vendor/cmaps/ with the Adobe BSD 3-Clause licence text reproduced there and this
section replaced by the attribution.

See vendor/README.md for the full vendoring posture, including the Adobe Glyph
List, which is absent for the same reason. The Core-14 AFM metrics were absent
for that reason too until decision #22; they are now present, under the APAFML
section above.
